# bridge_config — single per-CLI env file for `bridge-withdraw-e2e-cli`.
#
# WHAT IT IS
# ----------
# Consolidated env file for the withdraw-e2e CLI. Carries every parameter
# the CLI itself reads via clap `env` attrs (see `src/args.rs`), and
# nothing else. Single file; no per-mode split.
#
# The CLI is a standalone user-facing tool. It does not need — and this
# file deliberately does not carry — daemon-only settings
# (`BRIDGE_BOOTSTRAP_SEQNO`, `BRIDGE_ANCHOR_LEVEL`, `BRIDGE_BK_SET_CONFIG`).
# Those live in `../an-bridge-prover/L{1,2}_config/env` on whichever host
# runs `daemon-live`, which may be a different machine altogether.
#
# WHAT IT DELIBERATELY OMITS
# --------------------------
# `BURNER_PRIVATE_KEY` is NOT set here. Every operator brings their own
# Sepolia EVM key. Export it in your shell (or a personal, git-ignored
# env file) before invoking the CLI:
#
#   export BURNER_PRIVATE_KEY=0x…
#
# See §"Wallet setup and bridge config" in
# `docs/live_cli_withdraw_runbook.md` for wallet creation + Sepolia
# funding via the pk910 PoW or Google Cloud Web3 faucets. Never reuse a
# wallet that holds real funds; never commit the private key.
#
# HOW TO CONSUME
# --------------
#   cd crates/bridge-withdraw-e2e-cli
#   export BURNER_PRIVATE_KEY=0x…             # your own key
#   set -a && source config/bridge_config && set +a
#   ../an-bridge-prover/target/release/bridge-withdraw-e2e-cli withdraw ...
#
# Relative paths below are anchored to the working directory
# `crates/bridge-withdraw-e2e-cli/`.

# --- Ethereum side (Sepolia) --------------------------------------------------
RPC_URL=https://ethereum-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com

# --- Acki Nacki side (shellnet) -----------------------------------------------
BRIDGE_GQL_ENDPOINT=https://shellnet.ackinacki.org/graphql

# --- local dirs ---------------------------------------------------------------
# `params/` holds ~17 GB of SRS + per-circuit vk/pk files, shared with
# the bundle daemon. Do NOT wipe — keygen would re-burn ~7 min per
# circuit.
BRIDGE_PARAMS_DIR=../an-bridge-prover/params

# Optional — pk cache dir passed through to the C4 aggregator subprocess.
# The CLI defaults it to `$BRIDGE_PARAMS_DIR/pk_cache` if unset.
# BRIDGE_PK_CACHE_DIR=../an-bridge-prover/params/pk_cache

# Optional — where per-withdrawal idempotency state files live. Defaults
# to `$HOME/.bridge-withdraw-state/` when unset (per-user, survives
# tree moves; see `src/orchestrator.rs::default_state_dir`).
# BRIDGE_WITHDRAW_STATE_DIR=./withdraw-state

# --- SHPLONK aggregation (mandatory) ------------------------------------------
# The on-chain AckiNackiBridge verifier only accepts aggregated calldata.
# The CLI refuses to submit without both dirs resolving.
BRIDGE_AGGREGATOR_DIR=../bridge-evm-aggregator
BRIDGE_VERIFIERS_DIR=../../contracts/ethereum/verifiers

# --- Deploy target ------------------------------------------------------------
# Currently pinned to the shellnet team's L2-anchored (anchor_level=2)
# reference deploy on Sepolia. The server-side bundle relayer that
# advances this contract runs L2 only, so the CLI must be invoked with
# `--anchor-layer 2 --i-know-the-wait` against this address. See
# `docs/live_cli_withdraw_runbook.md` Case 8 Step L5.
#
# Advanced users who ran their own `deploy_bridge_bundle.sh` (see
# `../an-bridge-prover/bridge-relayer-daemon/docs/live_relayer_bridge_verifyBlock_runbook.md`)
# should overwrite this with the `BRIDGE_ADDRESS` from their own
# `L{1,2}_config/env`. L1 is testing-only; L2 is the production shape.
#
# Comment out to force the CLI to fail loudly ("missing required
# argument BRIDGE_ADDRESS") instead of silently connecting to the wrong
# bridge.
BRIDGE_ADDRESS=0x3fB082a905a895151224F6d93bD074E816338638
